RUBRIC:{"title":"SWEN3204 Assignment 2 – Marking Rubric","total":40,"criteria":[{"id":"C1","name":"Q1 Quality attributes","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"Two attributes that clearly matter most are chosen and justified from the scenario. Both scenarios have all six parts and both response measures are measurable."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"Suitable attributes are chosen with some justification. Scenarios are mostly complete but one is missing a part or has a response measure that is not measurable."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Attributes are named with little or no justification, or the scenarios are not in six-part form or are not measurable."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or irrelevant."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Q2 Architectural style","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"A clear recommendation justified by at least two trade-offs that are specific to the scenario (team size, load profile, known problems). The downside of the recommendation is acknowledged."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"A clear recommendation with two trade-offs, but one is generic or not linked to the scenario, or no downside is acknowledged."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"A recommendation with only one trade-off, or with generic textbook advantages and disadvantages only."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or no recommendation."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Q3 Availability calculation","weight":null,"max":8,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":7,"max":8,"desc":"Parts (a), (b) and (c) are all correct with working shown, to the requested precision."},{"label":"Proficient","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"The method is correct throughout but there is one arithmetic or rounding slip, or exactly one part is incorrect."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":4,"desc":"The series calculation is attempted but two or more parts are incorrect, or working is not shown."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or no correct element."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Q4 Resilience pattern","weight":null,"max":5,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":5,"desc":"An appropriate pattern is named, its mechanism is explained correctly, it is applied to the outage, and at least one drawback or tuning consideration is given."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"An appropriate pattern is named and explained correctly, but it is only loosely applied to the outage or no drawback or tuning consideration is given."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"A pattern is named but the explanation is incorrect or very thin."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or an unsuitable pattern."}]},{"id":"C5","name":"Q5 Consistency and availability","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"Both choices are justified, the CAP theorem is used correctly, and a suitable concrete technique is named for each case."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"Both choices are reasonable and techniques are named, but the CAP theorem is explained incorrectly or imprecisely, or one technique is missing."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Choices are stated with little justification, or the CAP theorem is not used."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted."}]},{"id":"C6","name":"Q6 Architecture decision record","weight":null,"max":5,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":5,"desc":"Context, Decision and Consequences are all present and specific to the scenario, with at least one positive and one negative consequence."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"All three sections are present but the consequences are one-sided (no negative consequence) or the context is generic."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"One or more sections are missing or the record does not describe a decision."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted."}]},{"id":"C7","name":"Communication and format","weight":null,"max":4,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Every answer is within 150 words, terminology is precise, the required headings are used and sources are cited in IEEE style."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":3,"desc":"Clear writing, but one answer exceeds the word limit or there are minor citation or formatting problems."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Several answers exceed the word limit, or the writing is hard to follow, or sources are not cited."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Format requirements ignored."}]}],"notes":"Award whole marks only. Each criterion is marked within the mark range of the level that best describes the answer."}
TASK:{"title":"SWEN3204 Software Architecture – Assignment 2: Short-Answer Questions","overview":"Answer six short questions applying architecture concepts to the CampusEats scenario. The assignment is worth 40 marks, including 4 marks for communication. Submit an individual, single-document response.","deliverables":["Answers to Questions 1–6, each under its required heading and in order.","Show calculations and working for all parts of Question 3.","Include IEEE-style citations for external sources and a reference list at the end."],"format":{"length":"Each answer must be at most 150 words; Question 3 calculations and working, and the reference list, are excluded from the limit.","structure":"Use the headings “Question 1” through “Question 6”, in order. Place the reference list at the end.","other":"Submit one document; this is an individual assignment. State any assumptions. Give availability as percentages to two decimal places and downtime in hours to one decimal place."},"requirements":[{"id":"R1","text":"Question 1: Identify the two most important quality attributes for CampusEats and justify each choice using the scenario. For each attribute, provide a quality attribute scenario with all six parts: source, stimulus, artefact, environment, response, and a measurable response measure."},{"id":"R2","text":"Question 2: Recommend an architectural style for the next 12 months (for example, monolith, modular monolith, or microservices). Justify the recommendation with at least two trade-offs specific to CampusEats."},{"id":"R3","text":"Question 3: Show your working. Calculate (a) order-placement availability using the component availabilities and independent failures, (b) expected order-placement downtime in hours per 30-day month, and (c) end-to-end availability and monthly downtime when a second independent payment provider of 99.5% availability is added active-active, with payment unavailable only when both providers are down."},{"id":"R4","text":"Question 4: Name one architectural resilience pattern that could contain the slow-payment-provider failure. Explain how it works and would limit the outage, and state at least one drawback or tuning consideration."},{"id":"R5","text":"Question 5: For menu browsing and for placing and paying for an order, choose whether to favour availability or consistency during a network partition. Justify each choice with reference to CAP theorem and name one concrete technique for each."},{"id":"R6","text":"Question 6: Write a short ADR for introducing a message queue between order payment and outlet notification. Include Context, Decision, and Consequences, with at least one positive and one negative consequence."},{"id":"R7","text":"State any assumptions made. Cite external sources in IEEE style and include the corresponding reference list; references do not count toward answer word limits."}]}
